# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The structures of the tuples that a simulation keeps from one activation
# of its entry to the next (D[activation-start], #294),
# Inputs/python_kept_tuples.py, on a GPU, where the incidence structures and
# the copies of the members are on the device: a sequence of starts against
# a simulation that builds every structure anew, with every structure that
# is taken also built, read back, and compared (MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: env MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES=1 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_kept_tuples.py starts %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double: 62 states, energies, and derivatives over 10 evaluations, an update, a commit, a checkpoint, and a run continued from it equal those of a simulation that builds its structures anew, to the bit; 5 structures taken where nothing moved, 5 built after the particles were ordered anew
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: 62 states, energies, and derivatives over 10 evaluations, an update, a commit, a checkpoint, and a run continued from it equal those of a simulation that builds its structures anew, to the bit; 5 structures taken where nothing moved, 5 built after the particles were ordered anew
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: two simulations and a frame evaluator of one program keep their structures apart; the evaluator builds its 5 once and takes them at every start after
# CHECK: GPU Mixed, not deterministic: the copies of the members on the device are taken with their structures, and the energy of the state is that of the first evaluation to rounding
# CHECK: kept tuples starts GPU passed
